## 📦 Setup & Installation

Ensure you have the required dependencies installed:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

**Key Dependencies:**
* `opencv-python==4.13.0.*`
* `numpy==1.23.5`
* `PyYAML>=6.0.3`
* `depthai==3.6.1`

## Must knows

1. If there's any error in launching the OAKD camera pipeline node, make sure your code uses v3 DepthAI API instead of v2, refer to its documentation: https://docs.luxonis.com/software-v3/depthai/

2. The camera, at the time of making this repository, is mounted in 180° rotation. That's why you'll observe almost all pipeline in code performing a 180° rotation to complement the hardware constraint (no place for camera cord). If any changes, just update the pipeline code and recalibrate the BEV polyon coords.

3. v1, v3, v4 nodes create their own OAKD pipeline. v5 instead subscribes to img/raw_rgb published by inference_node in object detection package. 

4. There are node codes available. To use them, just replace the main node code with code copied from the node scripts folder.

